1
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:09,218
[KIRKLAND whimpers]

2
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,011
Well? Don't just stand there!

3
00:00:11,053 --> 00:00:12,262
Hurry up and kill him!

4
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:14,223
Just run him through
with that knife!

5
00:00:14,264 --> 00:00:16,975
[KIRKLAND screams]

6
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,731
No. Mercy, sir!

7
00:00:21,772 --> 00:00:23,399
Why of all people
would you murder me

8
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,151
when I have done nothing to you?

9
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:41,208
Interesting,
this seems vastly different

10
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,043
from the original plan.

11
00:00:47,715 --> 00:00:51,427
For good reason, no doubt.
You have something else in mind.

12
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,639
Please forgive me, Brother.

13
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:59,059
This is going to leave you
exposed to public condemnation.

14
00:01:00,352 --> 00:01:03,564
Compared to the burden you're
trying to shoulder alone,

15
00:01:03,606 --> 00:01:06,275
it should be no trouble at all.

16
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,777
The aristocrats on that list

17
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:09,986
won't be the only
ones who suffer.

18
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:14,032
After you kill them, numerous
workers will be unemployed.

19
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:16,993
It's not difficult to
imagine what comes next.

20
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,872
The stampeding proletariat.

21
00:01:19,914 --> 00:01:23,292
[chuckles] Then again, I am
accustomed to dealing with,

22
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:26,044
shall we say,
those lacking in manners.

23
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:29,506
The mansion will be in safe
hands with me, Master William.

24
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:32,718
Grand. See to it,
Jack. Thank you.

25
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:35,429
[LOUIS]
Why is staying even necessary?

26
00:01:35,471 --> 00:01:39,975
We should leave here and go
into hiding; it would be safer.

27
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:44,480
[MORAN] Louis, William's
orders are absolute.

28
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:49,902
I'd strongly advise you
against questioning them.

29
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:51,946
[WILLIAM]
That's all there is to say.

30
00:01:55,449 --> 00:02:00,871
[WILLIAM] As of now, we're
moving on to the final problem.

31
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,220
What the devil
are you doing here?

32
00:03:40,262 --> 00:03:43,348
I don't remember asking
for any assistance from you.

33
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:48,478
You killed a man--

34
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,066
you're not in any
position to turn down help.

35
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:53,901
Why, Sherlock?

36
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:57,780
Milverton was beyond redemption

37
00:03:57,821 --> 00:04:00,908
and would never
serve a day behind bars.

38
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:03,035
Someone was bound to do it.

39
00:04:03,077 --> 00:04:05,412
It just happened
to be me. End of story.

40
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,040
And despite knowing
the burden it would

41
00:04:08,082 --> 00:04:12,669
place upon your shoulders,
you did it regardless?

42
00:04:12,711 --> 00:04:15,505
[HOLMES] I was aware of
what it would cost me.

43
00:04:15,547 --> 00:04:17,257
After killing him,

44
00:04:17,299 --> 00:04:20,469
I wouldn't be free to
pursue the Lord of Crime.

45
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:26,100
Look, Sherly, I'm afraid
if I tell you this,

46
00:04:26,141 --> 00:04:29,103
no good will come of it.

47
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:31,313
But for better or for worse.

48
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:32,606
It would appear you've managed

49
00:04:32,648 --> 00:04:35,109
to have gotten away with
committing the perfect crime.

50
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:38,904
[HOLMES gasps]
You don't mean...?

51
00:04:38,946 --> 00:04:42,407
Are you saying they haven't
recovered his body yet?

52
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,034
[MYCROFT]
Not only that--

53
00:04:44,076 --> 00:04:46,703
there were no
eyewitnesses at the scene,

54
00:04:46,745 --> 00:04:48,080
and because of the fire,

55
00:04:48,122 --> 00:04:51,667
no physical evidence such as
blood traces were left behind.

56
00:04:52,626 --> 00:04:56,088
In short, despite the
statement you made.

57
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:57,339
You're in the clear.

58
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:01,093
You cannot be charged for
murder on principle alone.

59
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:03,053
[LESTRADE]
What do you mean?

60
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:08,350
In any case, Mary needn't worry
about being threatened anymore.

61
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:10,769
She and John can
get married now.

62
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:12,228
So, it all worked out.

63
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,229
[door slams]

64
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:15,190
[WATSON]
You've some nerve!

65
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,401
[HOLMES]
John.

66
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,988
[WATSON grunts]

67
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:23,573
[WATSON] Sherlock Holmes
is officially a murderer,

68
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:24,616
but he wouldn't have been

69
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:27,577
if he waited for me
like he had promised!

70
00:05:27,619 --> 00:05:29,746
Just how did you
expect me to react?

71
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:32,332
Thrilled that you murdered
somebody?

72
00:05:32,374 --> 00:05:34,751
[HOLMES gasps]

73
00:05:34,793 --> 00:05:36,545
[HOLMES]
John.

74
00:05:38,047 --> 00:05:40,549
[WATSON] There is a chance
you will be released

75
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,676
without ever having
to go to trial,

76
00:05:42,718 --> 00:05:47,890
but even then, your actions will
haunt you the rest of your life!

77
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:51,434
You're a criminal,
shackled to the label forever,

78
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,146
and there's nothing you can do.

79
00:05:54,188 --> 00:06:05,281
Reflect on that for
one moment, you jackass!

80
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:07,659
[HOLMES grunts]

81
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:08,994
[MYCROFT chuckles]

82
00:06:09,036 --> 00:06:10,286
[knocking]

83
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:13,707
[POLICEMAN 23A] Inspector.
Forgive me, but it's urgent.

84
00:06:13,749 --> 00:06:15,042
What is it?

85
00:06:15,084 --> 00:06:18,045
[POLICEMAN 23A] Breaking news,
from all the major papers!

86
00:06:18,087 --> 00:06:21,090
The Lord of Crime's true
identity has been revealed!

87
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:24,509
And on top of that, an official
declaration of responsibility

88
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:26,887
arrived at the Yard
just moments ago.

89
00:06:26,929 --> 00:06:29,806
[HOLMES grunts]
Well, what did it say?

90
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:37,313
[WILLIAM]
To all the citizens of England.

91
00:06:37,355 --> 00:06:42,819
This morning, the life of Baron
Herschel was ended by me,

92
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:47,282
the Lord of Crime,
William James Moriarty.

93
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:50,702
[WILLIAM]
This is but the beginning.

94
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:54,539
I hereby declare that I will
slaughter the privileged class

95
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:58,293
and burn out the rot
that infests this nation.

96
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:02,380
None will be spared, not a soul.

97
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:08,762
[WILLIAM] For in truth,
no one can stop me.

98
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,432
[PARLAIMENT 23A]
We demand answers!

99
00:07:12,474 --> 00:07:15,227
Don't just silently
stand there, Lord Moriarty!

100
00:07:15,269 --> 00:07:16,728
[PARLAIMENT 23B]
As head of your family,

101
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,148
you have an obligation
to explain this!

102
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,316
[PARLAIMENT 23C] I'll wager
he had advanced knowledge

103
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:24,236
of these criminal acts!

104
00:07:24,278 --> 00:07:27,197
[PARLAIMENT 23A]
Say something, Lord Moriarty!

105
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:28,198
[TOWNSPEOPLE clamoring]

106
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,033
[MAN 23A]
The nobility may be one thing,

107
00:07:30,075 --> 00:07:34,746
but you killed Whitely in cold
blood! He was a decent man!

108
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:37,916
[MAN 23B]
Send William out, right now!

109
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:41,128
You've come in vain because
the master is not here!

110
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:43,088
Now, unless you have
actual business here,

111
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:45,674
I must ask you to leave!

112
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:49,303
[MORAN] They're reacting
exactly as predicted.

113
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:54,141
All of them. Parliament has
denounced the Moriarty name,

114
00:07:54,183 --> 00:07:56,935
while the citizens are
laying bare their anger

115
00:07:56,977 --> 00:07:59,980
at our front gate.

116
00:08:00,022 --> 00:08:02,191
You couldn't ask
for a more ideal start

117
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:03,984
to the "final problem."

118
00:08:04,026 --> 00:08:09,198
[LOUIS] All this time, I refused
to acknowledge the truth.

119
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:11,325
The plan only succeeds

120
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:14,328
with Brother's death
as the grand finale.

121
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:21,835
[LOUIS] I acted as
though I was unafraid.

122
00:08:21,877 --> 00:08:25,755
I shielded my heart, but now...

123
00:08:27,716 --> 00:08:31,136
[LOUIS] With the moment at hand,
I can no longer pretend.

124
00:08:32,095 --> 00:08:35,557
[LOUIS] Why must you
take this route, William?

125
00:08:35,598 --> 00:08:39,477
Brother, it's unfair you
should offer up your life

126
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:43,565
on behalf of
an ungrateful world.

127
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:47,736
They see you only
as a devil, where as I...

128
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:52,074
You're my world,
all that I have.

129
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:57,746
[WILLIAM]
Evening, Fred.

130
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:01,375
When I arrived at the mansion,

131
00:09:01,416 --> 00:09:05,045
all of the servants
had been knocked out.

132
00:09:05,087 --> 00:09:07,089
Your doing, I imagine.

133
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:14,012
[FRED] Guilty, they only took up
arms at their master's orders.

134
00:09:14,054 --> 00:09:17,057
I don't believe killing
anyone else was necessary.

135
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:22,396
But if I hadn't done it,
you would've killed them too!

136
00:09:22,437 --> 00:09:24,606
William, I know
you're carrying out

137
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,900
judgment that no one else can!

138
00:09:26,942 --> 00:09:29,194
But at the same time...

139
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:33,823
You're willing to die to take
responsibility for all of this?

140
00:09:37,119 --> 00:09:39,621
[WILLIAM]
Judgement, you say.

141
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:58,974
As I'm sure you're well aware,
I don't enjoy smoking.

142
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:01,643
Filthy habit that
pollutes the lungs.

143
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:05,147
[WILLIAM] These actions
that I've been undertaking,

144
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:08,317
I don't consider
them to be just.

145
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:10,235
If you want the whole truth,

146
00:10:10,277 --> 00:10:11,320
I don't believe a person

147
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:13,655
has the right to pass
judgement on another.

148
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,073
[gasps]

149
00:10:16,783 --> 00:10:18,952
[WILLIAM]
I am staggering

150
00:10:18,994 --> 00:10:22,622
beneath the ever-growing
weight of my sins.

151
00:10:22,664 --> 00:10:26,418
No matter how heinous
my victims may have been.

152
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,421
My hands are stained in scarlet.

153
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:32,341
[WILLIAM]
And no matter what I do,

154
00:10:32,382 --> 00:10:35,635
nothing will be able
to wash that blood away.

155
00:10:37,553 --> 00:10:40,265
[WILLIAM]
So, you see, my friend.

156
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:46,438
I'm more than ready to
put an end to all of this.

157
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:56,072
[FRED] There's no way I can stop
him, at least not on my own.

158
00:10:56,114 --> 00:11:00,869
At this point, all I can
do is appeal to him.

159
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,537
[FRED gasps]

160
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:08,418
[LOUIS]
Do you intend to betray Brother?

161
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:09,794
Why?

162
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,678
[LOUIS]
I understand now.

163
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,431
We knew this day would come.

164
00:11:21,473 --> 00:11:25,352
I'll accept any
punishment, except one.

165
00:11:25,394 --> 00:11:28,146
That's the thought
of William dying.

166
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:31,941
Even more so, the thought
of him wanting to die.

167
00:11:33,735 --> 00:11:35,070
[LOUIS]
I agree with you.

168
00:11:35,111 --> 00:11:36,530
[gasps]

169
00:11:41,076 --> 00:11:43,286
[LOUIS]
I hate to admit it,

170
00:11:43,328 --> 00:11:47,957
but we cannot intervene
without ruining the plan.

171
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:53,088
With this, it'll be the first
time I've gone against him.

172
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,839
Although,

173
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:59,010
if there is the slightest
chance of saving William's life.

174
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:02,389
I'll risk it, even if
it means betraying him.

175
00:12:02,431 --> 00:12:04,433
He mustn't die.

176
00:12:07,394 --> 00:12:11,481
[whimpers]

177
00:12:11,523 --> 00:12:13,649
[GLOVER]
Moriarty!

178
00:12:18,488 --> 00:12:22,658
I-Is anybody out there?
Someone, help me!

179
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:27,080
[whimpers]

180
00:12:27,122 --> 00:12:28,123
[gasps]

181
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:31,251
[EVAN, BOY 23A grunting]

182
00:12:33,545 --> 00:12:38,174
You hide behind your children?
Utterly despicable.

183
00:12:38,216 --> 00:12:40,176
Would you dare harm
a defenseless child?

184
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:41,136
Go right ahead!

185
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:43,597
[BOY 23A whimpering]

186
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:46,766
[EVAN whimpers]

187
00:12:48,768 --> 00:12:50,562
Son?

188
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:53,940
Kill me! Take my life
and spare theirs!

189
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:55,400
Please, sir, promise me

190
00:12:55,442 --> 00:12:58,945
you won't harm either
my father or my brother!

191
00:12:58,987 --> 00:13:03,908
I beg you!
Please, don't kill them!

192
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:09,664
[WILLIAM grunts]

193
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,666
[gasps]

194
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:14,169
[GLOVER groans]

195
00:13:17,339 --> 00:13:19,549
[EVAN gasps]

196
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,261
[EVAN]
No, Father!

197
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,347
You can't die!

198
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:29,434
[EVAN screams, sobs]

199
00:13:29,476 --> 00:13:32,354
[WILLIAM] Child, you were
bravely willing to sacrifice

200
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:35,231
your own life to save theirs.

201
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:39,653
If I deserve to be killed
by anyone, it's by you.

202
00:13:39,694 --> 00:13:42,947
Sadly, that's not to be.

203
00:13:42,989 --> 00:13:47,536
I can't die, at least not
until my work is finished.

204
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:52,541
I swear, you'll pay
for what you've done.

205
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:55,918
Moriarty!

206
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:04,302
[MORAN]
William, at this point,

207
00:14:04,344 --> 00:14:07,805
not even I can pull
the trigger on your behalf.

208
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:14,062
[MORAN]
No, only one can save you now.

209
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:33,373
[HOLMES] I see you,
William James Moriarty.

210
00:14:33,415 --> 00:14:37,126
The court ruled in favour
of a child from the slums.

211
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:40,296
That was Liam, I'm sure of it.

212
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:42,549
Later, he and his
brother were taken in

213
00:14:42,591 --> 00:14:46,344
by the Moriartys'
eldest son, Albert.

214
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:48,346
When the estate was set ablaze,

215
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:51,807
he replaced the
second son, William.

216
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:55,937
Which means, the three
brothers are the Lord of Crime.

217
00:14:55,978 --> 00:14:59,566
Co-conspirators from the start.

218
00:14:59,608 --> 00:15:04,779
Aboard the Noahtic, I caught
Liam's eye merely by chance.

219
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:08,824
The Drebber case was a test to
see if I could be of use to him.

220
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:14,038
[HOLMES] Behind each event
was a hidden agenda.

221
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:18,126
Liam playing the
role of Robin Hood.

222
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:23,757
Finally, the dots have
connected in my head.

223
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:26,968
A single red
thread linking them,

224
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:30,305
running through
each of the cases!

225
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,522
[HOLMES]
At long last,

226
00:15:39,564 --> 00:15:43,318
I am standing on
the same level as him.

227
00:15:50,366 --> 00:15:51,909
[VICTORIA]
Is that correct?

228
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,869
Even Marquis Glover?

229
00:15:53,911 --> 00:15:55,622
Then it's true,
and the Lord of Crime

230
00:15:55,664 --> 00:15:57,499
is indeed committed
to the destruction

231
00:15:57,540 --> 00:16:00,585
of this country's
privileged class.

232
00:16:00,627 --> 00:16:04,631
Clearly, he wants us to know
nothing will abate his killing.

233
00:16:04,673 --> 00:16:08,384
He can strike anyone,
anywhere, any time.

234
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:10,804
No one is safe.

235
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,139
We must be quick.

236
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:16,267
Bring Sherlock Holmes
here at once, Director.

237
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,562
Majesty.

238
00:16:27,529 --> 00:16:29,989
[HOLMES grunts]

239
00:16:37,622 --> 00:16:41,000
I ask your forgiveness, please.

240
00:16:41,042 --> 00:16:42,960
Though it was extreme,

241
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:44,796
I based my decision
on what I thought

242
00:16:44,838 --> 00:16:47,465
would benefit you the most.

243
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:51,761
I admit, I wasn't concerned with
the consequences I would face.

244
00:16:51,803 --> 00:16:54,013
But a little more thought--

245
00:16:54,055 --> 00:16:55,264
No.

246
00:16:55,306 --> 00:16:58,685
Much more thought should
have gone into this.

247
00:16:58,727 --> 00:17:04,315
Just as I have a need for you,
I forgot you have a need for me.

248
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:06,776
As long as we share that bond,

249
00:17:06,818 --> 00:17:10,613
I should be more aware of
how my actions affect you.

250
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:14,325
From now on, I will
handle myself better.

251
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:16,035
I promise.

252
00:17:23,084 --> 00:17:23,918
[WATSON]
Look at me.

253
00:17:23,959 --> 00:17:25,294
[gasps]

254
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,547
[WATSON]
Very well.

255
00:17:27,589 --> 00:17:31,175
Now, I have something
to say to you.

256
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:35,096
I'm thankful... for you
saving Mary and our wedding.

257
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:38,433
I do mean that, my friend.

258
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,059
John.

259
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:43,396
Right.

260
00:17:43,438 --> 00:17:47,400
Come now, let's be off.
Her Majesty awaits us.

261
00:17:47,442 --> 00:17:50,486
Imagine, late for the Queen.

262
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:51,738
Hm?

263
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:54,824
Before we go, you'll need a tie.

264
00:17:58,787 --> 00:18:00,538
I thank you both for coming.

265
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,875
Our nation is in peril
and needs you.

266
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:05,501
Mister Sherlock Holmes,

267
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:09,255
and you, Doctor John
Hamish Watson.

268
00:18:09,297 --> 00:18:13,217
It is an honour to make your
acquaintance, Your Majesty.

269
00:18:24,687 --> 00:18:27,523
[MYCROFT] That was rather
bold of you, Sherly.

270
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:35,698
Liam risked his life to
create the current situation.

271
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:38,868
This opportunity
won't come around again.

272
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,787
If things do not change now,

273
00:18:40,829 --> 00:18:44,039
this country of ours
will be finished.

274
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:47,460
Well, it seems you've finally
realized his intention.

275
00:18:47,502 --> 00:18:49,128
Took you long enough.

276
00:18:49,170 --> 00:18:51,213
[HOLMES gasps]

277
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:54,175
[HOLMES] It sounds as
though both of us have.

278
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,721
Good-bye.

279
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:09,023
[MYCROFT] Sherly, don't
get yourself killed.

280
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,866
[HOLMES]
Miss Hudson.

281
00:19:19,868 --> 00:19:22,495
Welcome back home.
We missed you.

282
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:26,123
[HOLMES]
Too quiet, eh?

283
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:27,416
[HUDSON giggles]

284
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:32,171
Ah! Almost forgot; a telegram
arrived for you earlier.

285
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:54,944
[HOLMES] The third son of
the Moriarty family, Louis.

286
00:19:54,986 --> 00:19:57,112
And you're from the Hope affair,

287
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:59,741
disguised yourself
convincingly as an old woman.

288
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:00,700
Your name is?

289
00:20:00,742 --> 00:20:02,577
Fred Porlock, Mister Holmes.

290
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:07,707
[LOUIS] There's only one reason
I would meet you in this manner.

291
00:20:07,749 --> 00:20:08,917
The truth is--

292
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:11,252
[HOLMES] You want me to
save Liam's life, correct?

293
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:12,336
[gasps]

294
00:20:12,378 --> 00:20:14,505
[FRED gasps]

295
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:15,798
[HOLMES]
In order for Liam's plan

296
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:20,469
to achieve its maximum effect,
it requires him to die.

297
00:20:21,721 --> 00:20:24,098
Considering the timing and how
you reached out to me directly,

298
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:26,601
that must mean one thing.

299
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:29,437
Your brother,
he won't feign his demise.

300
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:32,023
He truly means to end his life.

301
00:20:32,065 --> 00:20:34,233
Are you going to help us or not?

302
00:20:34,275 --> 00:20:35,150
Answer me!

303
00:20:35,192 --> 00:20:38,446
Rest assured,
I intend to save him.

304
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:39,405
[LOUIS gasps]

305
00:20:39,447 --> 00:20:43,367
[HOLMES]
After all, Liam is my friend.

306
00:20:47,038 --> 00:20:49,123
As of now, that's all I can say.

307
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:51,084
Are you satisfied?

308
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:57,423
[HOLMES]
You've actually reassured me.

309
00:20:57,465 --> 00:21:01,218
There's more to family
than just flesh and blood.

310
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,012
Mister Holmes,

311
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:07,892
we are more than prepared to
accept any punishment, any.

312
00:21:07,934 --> 00:21:10,812
But please make sure
you save my brother's life.

313
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:15,066
Leave him to me.

314
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:18,272
I've come with a request.

315
00:23:18,313 --> 00:23:21,859
Regarding the story of
Sherlock Holmes' nemesis.

316
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:25,113
Would you kindly
bring it to a close?

317
00:23:25,154 --> 00:23:27,073
As you wish.

318
00:23:34,872 --> 00:23:37,499
[WILLIAM] Next time on
Moriarty the Patriot  :

319
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:40,128
"The Final Problem, Act Two."
